{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1354814-why-is-the-children-of-gaia-revised-tribebook-so-reviled","id":1354814,"title":"Why is the Children of Gaia Revised Tribebook so reviled?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-13T13:48:27-08:00","id":1354814,"title":"Why is the Children of Gaia Revised Tribebook so reviled?","content":"Hello All,<br /> <br /> I'd like to ask for your oppinion.<br /> <br /> I heard/read from multimple sources that the CoG Revised is bad. Very, very bad.<br /> <br /> I've never read it, so I have zero opponion, but I'm intrested.<br /> <br /> What were the flaws? Theme? Inconsistency? Real life problems (drugs, homosexualty, etc.) handled badly or what?<br /> <br /> Thank you,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T14:12:47-08:00","id":1354819,"title":"","content":"It took some hard swerves away from setting consistency. There was a rite that could turn a human or wolf into kinfolk, a rite that gave some unspecified bonus to &quot;resist&quot; frenzy by having sex in Crinos (typically with other Garou), and a rite that may or might not be routinely used to kick BSDs back into being Gaian via the practice of sin-eating. That's two shortcuts that undercut some pretty heavy struggles in the game, and one presentation of first tenet violation as a common, if underground, practice that doesn't even have any actual mechanical effects associated with it.<br /> <br /> The story sections were also party to some serious pitfalls, like concentrating on Woodstock (with an out in the open battle with BSDs that leap out of burning porta-potties), as well as the point of view characters having terrible hot takes on various subjects. Overall, the struggle for peace presented in the book was a bit too successful for the WoD. It also introduced some historical personalities as CoGs, in a break from WW having typically shied away from this after the days of Vampire Al Capone and hidden nazi war criminals, though admittedly, the author didn't choose a particularly grandiose bunch, so it's not as bad in this respect as early Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T14:14:59-08:00","id":1354820,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest problem is that it is fairly dull and uninspired, doing nothing to advance the tribe beyond its &quot;furry hippy&quot; stereotype. That is my opinion in a nutshell, at least. I may post something more in depth later, time permitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T18:10:11-08:00","id":1355098,"title":"","content":"Apparently white Middle class Liberals are meant be be ancient tribe that dates back to Summer or something.. That is to say they are painfully American and painfully dated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T19:24:21-08:00","id":1355106,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I may have to reconsider buying Children of Gaia. It\u2019s unlikely that SJWs would have existed in ancient Sumer, and getting sexual with other Garou is a serious violation of the Litany. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T21:44:37-08:00","id":1355123,"title":"","content":"My own take on the tribe is that they are one of the Garou Nation's three tribes of leadership, along side the Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords, likely originating with the first Garou who opposed the Impergium (or at least this is a somewhat self agrandizing story that is popular within the tribe). But where the Fangs favor an appeal to a divine mandate of greatness and the Lords favor realpolitik, the CoG tend towards a mix of diplomacy and righteous example (and more than a little passive agressive moralizing and occasional totalitarianism bullying thrown in). Ultimately, they really want to overthrow the Silver Fangs and take over the Garou Nation, eventually turning them all into one big tribe again. Their ideas of &quot;non-violence&quot; isn't the same as that of humans, as Rage and their duty as Gaia's Fangs make that impossible. Instead, their ideal is that Garou should never fight each other, at least never to the death (non-combat challenges are preferred for settling disputes), should never abuse kinfolk or really even anyone (it violates the Littany), and should when possible try to heal those poisoned by the Wyrm, with mercy killing as a final resort to end suffering. Really, of all tribes, they should have a high level rite that gives a chance for removing a bane from a fomori (even if the victim dies, their soul is saved). But BSDs should require Eberus or a one off Gaian miracle to be saved. And while the tribe should be one of the most accepting of metis, they shouldn't be encouraging Garou incest. (Also Garou cant have sex in crinos, as their genitals retract inside their body. So a rite depending on that is silly.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T05:57:27-08:00","id":1355163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1354814-why-is-the-children-of-gaia-revised-tribebook-so-reviled?p=1355123#post1355123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Garou cant have sex in crinos, as their genitals retract inside their body.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that isn't silly?<br /> <br /> Iirc rev. ST Handbook's FAQ section simply stated that genitals don't grow in proportion with the rest of the body, comparing homid to Crinos. That means that a crinos has a penis and balls, probably covered by fur, if male. It also explicitly states that the 1st Edition artwork female crinos with breasts aren't canonial anymore. Being between human and wolf the crinos has probably several tits, like a wolf would, but they are not proportional either, because Crinos isn't to nurture.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T06:13:11-08:00","id":1355165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1354814-why-is-the-children-of-gaia-revised-tribebook-so-reviled?p=1355163#post1355163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that isn't silly?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's to protect them from damage. Crinos is a combat form, and that is one of its features. Ethan Skemp used to point this out fairly frequently on various forums and mailing lists when he was developer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T13:02:10-08:00","id":1355245,"title":"","content":"Given the metis Thrall of the Wyrm condition and consequences, they clearly can have sex in Crinos, but given the heightened anger and apparent sensitivity to stress, it's probably really, really difficult under &quot;typical&quot; conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T13:25:04-08:00","id":1355249,"title":"","content":"The Children of Gaia have rarely been surved well by their write-ups and while I do like them, one generally has to provide headcanon and homebrew material for them, like No One of Consequence did above to make them as cool as they have the potential of being.<br /> <br /> Aside from the infamous issues already mentioned above like the Clouds sex rite, the issue of a Woodstock battle ground, I had issues with most of the books layout. The history chapter is convoluted and out of order which could be excusable if, to put it bluntly, the writing was better but instead it's just a confusing mess that's irritating to read and flip through for a coherent narrative or to dig up potential plot hooks or narrative crumbs.<br /> <br /> The section of tribal culture continues its convoluted writing style, brushing over things in a way that was personally frustrating to read, varying between preachy and under-explanatory in the worse places. Also, this is a personal pet peeve, but for Gaia's Sake, these books follow a very useful outline, how do you fuck that up and leave out a section on the auspices entirely?!<br /> <br /> *sigh*<br /> <br /> That aside, the books biggest failure is that it's ironically perhaps the most fleshed out satire of the Children of Gaia we have written. If they'd released this with a note from a Nuwishu who'd infiltrated Black Dog as a prank as prologue, this might have been comedy gold... assuming there was also a decent tribebook along with it.<br /> <br /> The revised tribebook feeds into the worst tribal stereotypes, making them out as the liberal peacenik hippies of werewolf who would have died out in the 70s and that's a genuine shame because there is such potential here.<br /> <br /> They could have told a story of the ideals of cooperation and peace. What it means to be willing to do in the name of creating peace and stability for your people. The hard compromise that come along with cooperation. The fear of walking a road to hell paved with good intentions.<br /> <br /> The hippie movement and 90s white suburban activism could both have been incorporated into that weave, with positives and negatives drawn from both. Instead they got so absorbed into preaching as holier-then-thou, stumbling over themselves to appear inclusive and diverse without fully exploring the ramifications and reasons for that, and being so self-righteous without earning that right; that they turn the Children of Gaia into a parody of themselves.<br /> <br /> Which is a genuine shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T19:57:02-08:00","id":1355326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1354814-why-is-the-children-of-gaia-revised-tribebook-so-reviled?p=1355106#post1355106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I may have to reconsider buying Children of Gaia. It\u2019s unlikely that SJWs would have existed in ancient Sumer, and getting sexual with other Garou is a serious violation of the Litany. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No.. actual Social Justice Warriors taken NONIRONICALLY would have been a good push for the tribe. There are all sorts of directions they could have been taken in that weren't complete jokes. Its like if the SIlver Fang book written as if the Tribe was basically the Knights and King from Monty Python and the Holy grail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T22:54:49-08:00","id":1355342,"title":"","content":"If, in some alternative universe, I had been asked to write the revised CoG book, I suspect that the history chapter would have started with ending of the Impergium and the original pact with Unicorn (probably with some mention that what the totem looked like back then isn't exactly the medieval horse we think of, but more like a single horned auroch as seen in ancient Indus Valley seals, possibly having some sort of connection to the lost Apis), before getting into stories about said Indus Valley Civilization and ancient Sumer (which was as much Warders turf as it was theirs), before the Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs rolled in with the proto IndoEuropeans. A bit about the Classical World and these strange new philosophies and monotheic religions. Some Dark Ages stuff* and how they have a lot more going on then than you would think. The whole Renaissance/Age of Discovery/Enlightenment period and initial contacts with the 3 Brothers, various premodern utopian movements, and an emphasis on the Great Awakenings. And likely a big aside about why classical liberalism was very appealing to the tribe, but also why the siren song of 20th century progressive totalitarianism - what is arguably the modern Weaver Patriarch/Big Brother - continues to be attractive to many. The 20th century should be considered a tragic failing, with a hemoclysm of industrialized state sponsored mass murder usually in service of creating an earthly utopia, brutal wars, and a general lack of empathy toward others. Even whatever hopeful idealism American CoG felt in the triumphs of the 60s pretty much devolved into the Days of Rage, National Malaise, and Me Decade of the 70s. I would argue that what the world needed on the eve of the Apocalypse, and what the CoG can offer more than anyone, is empathy. The simple idea that other people are worthwhile and deserving of basic respect, compassion and understanding, even if we disagree with or don't like them very much. <br /> Culture wise, I'd probably have played off the contrast and contradictions of the previous statement with my earlier comments about them wanting to be in charge of the Garou Nation, making this the major source of conflict (political, emotional, internal, etc.) within the tribe. There would have to be a relatively sizable section about adoption - Garou who decide to renounce one tribe and join the CoG, as well as their taking in of unwanted metis, male Garou who would otherwise be Furies, and probably Fangs who aren't pure enough, and maybe even Wendigo who aren't pure enough either (though the Uktena may call dibs). I would downplay the whole free love vibe. Yes, sex is fun and healthy, and there are a lot of fertility rites to help pop out lots of wolf and human kin, and no one really cares if you are gay or the like (as long as you at least make a token effort to try to breed. Garou incest is still frowned upon, but I would likely concede to some sort of sectretive rite which allows for mental dream sex or something. Camps would include the Servants of Unicorn/Unicorn Crusade, Patient Deed and Imminent Strike as embodiments of the tribe's inner conflicts, and a retooling or replacement of others. At least one camp devoted to spiritual, emotional and physical healing of people, the land, spirits and others who have been hurt or damaged. Atleast one focused on fertility and matchmaking (not just among garou and kin, but for humans, endangered species, and any others that need someone in their life). And one martial one drawing heavily on Morihei Ueshiba's The Art of Peace** and the ideals of defending the helpless and innocent as a key aspect of being Gaia's Fangs. <br /> No idea what the templates would be, aside from a homid ahroun martial artist devoted to the idea that the only rational purpose for mastering violence is to abolish it. <br /> <br /> *My Dark Ages games have long been built around the idea that the events of the loss of the Silver Crown and the fall of House Winter Snow happens in the early 12th century, and the power vacuum and disruption has led to a three way civil war between the Falcon Banner, the Army of Thunder, and the Unicorn Crusade. I just like conflict for a more dynamic setting.<br /> <br /> **I highly recommend this little book for anyone interested in the CoG mindset. Also, oddly, The Seven Habits of Highly Effective People .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T06:50:38-08:00","id":1355392,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2715\" data-vbnamecard=\"2715\">Lian</a> you're right. That would've been cool.<br /> <br /> It's weird. I can Mention your name on my desktop but it doesn't work on my phone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T07:26:49-08:00","id":1356088,"title":"","content":"It also has a lot of REALLY weird stuff otherwise. Like an open homid-lupus gay relationship that legit sounds predatory from the lupus' part. Glabro sex dungeons,etc.<br /> <br /> And the worst thing about the crinos sex rite? It has NO mechanics. None. Now, I am not a prude about stuff like that at all. But it is fetishistic stuff in a RP book with no chance to fade-to-black to just roll the rite.<br /> <br /> It is also, as Lian said, VERY white middle-class american focused. As in, it really does not even consider other countries as valid places for Children of Gaia to exist in. Now, there are many tribebooks similar to CoG revised in that, but CoG Revised truly hammers in on the white middle-class hippie mentality over actually exploring ancestral Children of Gaia. It literally reads likke the tribe began existing once america was discovered.<br /> <br /> There is also a scene where a challenge over the disbanding of camps is rejected because 'peace, man.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 12-20-2019, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T12:00:36-08:00","id":1356137,"title":"","content":"I always figured that the Middle East and its surrounding areas (North Africa, Southwest Asia) would have been really interesting places to explore CoG culture. Especially influences from or ties with the Bahai faith, the various Sufi orders, historical Zoroastrianism and its surviving practitioners, and certain aspects of Yazidism, among others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T18:01:30-08:00","id":1356205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1354814-why-is-the-children-of-gaia-revised-tribebook-so-reviled?p=1356137#post1356137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always figured that the Middle East and its surrounding areas (North Africa, Southwest Asia) would have been really interesting places to explore CoG culture. Especially influences from or ties with the Bahai faith, the various Sufi orders, historical Zoroastrianism and its surviving practitioners, and certain aspects of Yazidism, among others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, and also just do a lot of the same stuff that TB:Fenrir revised and ESPECIALLY TB: Silent Striders revised did. De-mystify the tribe and really go into the meat of their beliefs.<br /> <br /> I mean, you got the Crusades, the Spanish Moors, the Ottoman Empire and many other cool things to use as sources of culture. Dark Ages books actually DID use those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T22:16:30-08:00","id":1356236,"title":"","content":"Since Tribebook: CoG Revised is so bad, which Tribe books are good? like which ones are the ones to reccomend to someone trying to get more in depth with their character's tribe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11112-brothermouse","name":"BrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T00:17:34-08:00","id":1356251,"title":"","content":"There should be some Hengeyokai variant for COG. They are all about bringing peace to the Nation.. and there's this multiFera group working together, hell that could be a big divide among the Tribe whether or what is a priority. Similarly they should be in the Ahadi. This is their thing and they have no connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T00:55:42-08:00","id":1356259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrotherMouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1354814-why-is-the-children-of-gaia-revised-tribebook-so-reviled?p=1356236#post1356236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Tribebook: CoG Revised is so bad, which Tribe books are good? like which ones are the ones to reccomend to someone trying to get more in depth with their character's tribe?</div> </div> </div> </div>The best revised tribebook is Silent Striders revised, followed by Glass Walkers and Get of Fenris. Red Talons, Silver Fangs, Fianna and most others do a decent enough job portraying their tribes. Wendigo even has credits from Nunavut's libraries, so it is that well researched.<br /> <br /> COG revised is bad because of the way it handles its content, more than anything else. Supplement pipeline was in effect when it was made, so I'm guessing when people noticed its... issues, it was far too late to fix things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T13:47:44-08:00","id":1356366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1354814-why-is-the-children-of-gaia-revised-tribebook-so-reviled?p=1356251#post1356251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should be some Hengeyokai variant for COG. They are all about bringing peace to the Nation.. and there's this multiFera group working together, hell that could be a big divide among the Tribe whether or what is a priority. Similarly they should be in the Ahadi. This is their thing and they have no connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original CoG book made an offhand mention of them being in ancient China, but that was never followed up on to my knowledge. My own personal headcanon is that they arrived in small numbers during the Yellow River civilizations and their totem was later tied to local qilin legends, with the influx of Buddhism being a big deal for them, but the long period of regional strife - the Taiping Rebellion, the Boxer Uprising, the Warlord Period, WW2, the civil war, the Great Leap Forward, the Cultural Revolution - and Communist oppression being especially hard on their ideals. I've always seen them as big boosters of the Beast Courts, mainly as Lanterns, Pillars, and Courtiers, especially among the court of Ambassadors. But that is just me. <br /> <br /> As for the Ahadi, I think it would be interesting to have a small sect of racially diverse South African CoG who eagerly want to join the alliance, but the other southern African factions being warry of them for various reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T14:10:31-08:00","id":1356371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1354814-why-is-the-children-of-gaia-revised-tribebook-so-reviled?p=1356366#post1356366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The original CoG book made an offhand mention of them being in ancient China, but that was never followed up on to my knowledge. My own personal headcanon is that they arrived in small numbers during the Yellow River civilizations and their totem was later tied to local qilin legends, with the influx of Buddhism being a big deal for them, but the long period of regional strife - the Taiping Rebellion, the Boxer Uprising, the Warlord Period, WW2, the civil war, the Great Leap Forward, the Cultural Revolution - and Communist oppression being especially hard on their ideals. I've always seen them as big boosters of the Beast Courts, mainly as Lanterns, Pillars, and Courtiers, especially among the court of Ambassadors. But that is just me.<br /> <br /> As for the Ahadi, I think it would be interesting to have a small sect of racially diverse South African CoG who eagerly want to join the alliance, but the other southern African factions being warry of them for various reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hengeyokai also placed the BGs and CoGs in the Beast Courts, with qilin as a local appearance of Unicorn, but for whatever reason, any mention of them ended up squashed in favor of marketing the Hakken and Stargazers, to the point that WoD: Blood and Silk tried to make the Hakken a thing around the time of Huangdi, or at least a legend that maps the Beast Courts/Wan Xian struggle onto Huangdi vs. Chiyou, and get this, Chiyou was supposed to be Hakken in this story, as well as the only change ever condemned to Yomi for... (looks at file) defying heaven in attacking the Wan Xian, even though they had lost heaven's favor by this point.<br /> <br /> Reason #2 why the text of Blood and Silk is not to be trusted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T15:47:49-08:00","id":1356382,"title":"","content":"For some reason - I honestly forgot why atm - I've always viewed the Hakken as being primarily Japanese and Korean, with the ones that are Chinese being largely from the areas north of the Great Wall (Manchuria, outer Mongolia), and then the Mongolian ones. I think this is because I have long tended to associate the Shadow Lords with the IndoEuropeans and Grandfather Thunder with their various sky-thunder gods*, including central Asian Tengrism. I am not enough of an anthropology expert to say if gods like Leigong, Raiden, or their Korean counterpart share this possible common origin, but in the WoD, the idea that they all derive from Grandfather Thunder seems possible. Also, it allows me to exercise my longstanding GIJoe fanboyism by having the Arashikage be one of the dominant Hakken clans. (My headcanon is also that there are still hidden and carefully tended populations of Japanese and Hokkaido wolf kinfolk, the same way there are still wolves in the British Isles in the WoD.)<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I tend to view the Glasswalkers as the more southern Chinese tribe, with the Bone Gnawers and Children of Gaia along the eastern areas, and the Silent Striders in the west/northwest, the Stargazers centered in Tibet and the Himalayas but spread across Asia, and the Red Talons mostly in the west and north. <br /> <br /> *Including Indra and Zeus, which gives me a lot to play with in India and the Mediterranean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T16:11:46-08:00","id":1356389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1354814-why-is-the-children-of-gaia-revised-tribebook-so-reviled?p=1356382#post1356382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason - I honestly forgot why atm - I've always viewed the Hakken as being primarily Japanese and Korean, with the ones that are Chinese being largely from the areas north of the Great Wall (Manchuria, outer Mongolia), and then the Mongolian ones. I think this is because I have long tended to associate the Shadow Lords with the IndoEuropeans and Grandfather Thunder with their various sky-thunder gods*, including central Asian Tengrism. I am not enough of an anthropology expert to say if gods like Leigong, Raiden, or their Korean counterpart share this possible common origin, but in the WoD, the idea that they all derive from Grandfather Thunder seems possible. Also, it allows me to exercise my longstanding GIJoe fanboyism by having the Arashikage be one of the dominant Hakken clans. (My headcanon is also that there are still hidden and carefully tended populations of Japanese and Hokkaido wolf kinfolk, the same way there are still wolves in the British Isles in the WoD.)<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I tend to view the Glasswalkers as the more southern Chinese tribe, with the Bone Gnawers and Children of Gaia along the eastern areas, and the Silent Striders in the west/northwest, the Stargazers centered in Tibet and the Himalayas but spread across Asia, and the Red Talons mostly in the west and north.<br /> <br /> *Including Indra and Zeus, which gives me a lot to play with in India and the Mediterranean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arashikage comes up in Dragons of the East, as both a surname of a Hakken giving a quote on whether or not kin mages can stick with the family and a consumer products company. Presumably, the family is in control of the conglomerate. Never gets name-dropped anywhere else, I think. Long story short, apparently someone else wanted to indulge in GI Joe fanboyism, too, and they wrote it into the game.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers, I'd say, are everywhere. It's their thing - wherever you dump garbage and later abandon, where no one wants to go, you find the Gnawers. They and the Ratkin are basically omnipresent around human settlements in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T17:53:01-08:00","id":1356406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1354814-why-is-the-children-of-gaia-revised-tribebook-so-reviled?p=1356382#post1356382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(My headcanon is also that there are still hidden and carefully tended populations of Japanese and Hokkaido wolf kinfolk, the same way there are still wolves in the British Isles in the WoD.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this explicit in ww20 I think its either in Changing Breeds or Rage across the world. And honestly it makes sense since.. wolves IRL are &quot;Cryptids&quot; in Japan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T20:06:33-08:00","id":1356421,"title":"","content":"I vaguely recall my impressions about the Chinese Bone Gnawers/Wang Tong(?) coming from the coast's huge population density as well as the presence of the Hakka ethno-cultural group. But their counterpart to the western Hillfolk are probably scattered all over China and surrounding areas.<br /> <br /> I've not read any WW20 material, but my impression after seeing Dog Soldiers was that if Scotland has areas that remote and isolated, I'm not only unsurprised at stories of wolf survivors, I'm kind of amazed they don't have stories about lost tribes of Scottish Bigfoots riding around on woolly mammoths and battling giant trolls the way they do in Canada. (not really)<br /> <br /> And Dragons of the East also has a Simpsons reference in the Ratkin bit.<br /> <br /> Back to the Children of Gaia, I've always wondered what they look like culturally in South America. The locals, that is, not the Amazon War emigres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T20:21:44-08:00","id":1356424,"title":"","content":"I had another CHildren of Gaia thought taken from the book. The Book functionally treats them as if they came into existence in the 20th century even if it claims greater history. Well what if we did take it the other way? What if the Children of Gaia were a Tribe created in relatively Modern times? The Warders can be responsible for ending the Imperigum. What if the COG come into existance Post the Death of the Bunyip? People through out the nation sick of the constant wars and bickering with Unicorn coming forward to claim them?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T20:46:58-08:00","id":1356428,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Interesting. It might upend certain parts of the setting, but I'm just not sure what at the moment. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T19:29:15-08:00","id":1356571,"title":"","content":"The biggest issue with a new tribe coming into being in recent historical times is that it raises the idea of why can't there be new tribes arising now. Then you'll have PCs trying to start a new tribe of Raven, Boar, Fox or any other totem. By having all the tribes originate in the distant past - in mythical times not subject to the scrutiny of rational history - you preserve the idea that it takes mythic quests to achieve that status. Perhaps even implying that in today's world with a strong Gauntlet, it may not even be possible to do so. These kinds of quests really aren't properly handled by the game mechanics.<br /> <br /> I think Legendary ranks are problematic enough without adding the idea that characters can quest to establish new tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 12-23-2019, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-23T14:59:16-08:00","id":1356699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1354814-why-is-the-children-of-gaia-revised-tribebook-so-reviled?p=1356571#post1356571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest issue with a new tribe coming into being in recent historical times is that it raises the idea of why can't there be new tribes arising now. Then you'll have PCs trying to start a new tribe of Raven, Boar, Fox or any other totem. By having all the tribes originate in the distant past - in mythical times not subject to the scrutiny of rational history - you preserve the idea that it takes mythic quests to achieve that status. Perhaps even implying that in today's world with a strong Gauntlet, it may not even be possible to do so. These kinds of quests really aren't properly handled by the game mechanics.<br /> <br /> I think Legendary ranks are problematic enough without adding the idea that characters can quest to establish new tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue 1e strongly implied a player COULD do that so I really don't see the issue. I Mean do the Tremere mean every PC is going to go form theirown clan? Two Traditions formed in the last century, it doesn't push pcs to go form theirown Tradition. One could even make a whole &quot;There must always be 13 tribes as a thing&quot; if you're really worried about that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T18:09:58-08:00","id":1357144,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Children of Gaia and totems, I have kind of mixed feelings about the ones in the tribe books. The original only gave up The New World Trinity (Eagle, Dove, and Turkey), which I think is an interesting idea, but not one I think works all that well for Werewolf. (It feels like something that would fit better with certain types of Dreamspeakers and modernest unawakened shamans.) The new edition gives us Black Unicorn (which originally appeared in Axis Mundi), Father Mule (which again is an idea I like, I'm just not 100% sold on it being a &quot;CoG&quot; totem rather than a Garou Nation wide one), and Sea Otter (which I'd just as soon be just-Otter). <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd have gone with an in depth look at Unicorn, including it's incarnations/aspects/brood-members like Black Unicorn, Qilin, Al-mi'raj, Shadhavar, Rhinoceros, Auroch, and White Horse. Then some of the more conceptual totems such as The People (from Players Guide to the Garou), and American Dream (where the Bone Gnawers seen it as a symbol of sanctuary for the poor and oppressed and the Silent Striders as a symbol of a homeland for the dispossessed and outcasts, the Children of Gaia see it as a symbol of the hope for equality, tolerance, and liberty), as well as the celestial totem Lu-Bat. Probably also some notice about totems like Bear, Bull, Goat, Butterfly, and West Wind. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure which new totems I'd include. I like the idea of Otter. Probably Qilin and Shadhavar. Black Unicorn and maybe White Horse as counterparts. Dove maybe. West Wind. Shepherd? Ram?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}